WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.530
Two diseases can leave
joints stiff and painful.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.820
Both are called arthritis.

3
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.480
One usually strikes weight-bearing joints:

4
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.100
knees and hips.

5
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.230
The other strikes the small
joints of the hands and feet,

6
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.170
on both sides of the body.

7
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.620
Yet only one of them is treated with
drugs that damp down the immune system.

8
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.380
So why calm the immune
system for one disease,

9
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.880
but not the other?

10
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:28.280
In this mission, you'll look inside two
damaged joints and compare what has gone

11
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.240
wrong.

12
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:35.530
Then you'll judge a real trial: 242
growing teenagers with curved spines,

13
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.780
and whether wearing a brace helped.

14
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.830
Your mission: explain why only one of
these joint diseases is treated by calming

15
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.040
the immune system.
